The marks in this folder are the languages a file's extension names (item 547).

Simple Icons (https://simpleicons.org), version 16.35.0, released under CC0 1.0 Universal
(https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/): each file is the icon's path alone, with the brand's colour as the
file's fill (the colour Simple Icons gives it), unchanged: c.svg, clojure.svg, cmake.svg, cplusplus.svg, css.svg, dart.svg, docker.svg, dotnet.svg, elixir.svg, gnubash.svg, go.svg, gradle.svg, haskell.svg, html5.svg, javascript.svg, json.svg, jupyter.svg, kotlin.svg, lua.svg, markdown.svg, openjdk.svg, perl.svg, php.svg, python.svg, r.svg, ruby.svg, rust.svg, sass.svg, scala.svg, sqlite.svg, svelte.svg, svg.svg, swift.svg, toml.svg, typescript.svg, vuedotjs.svg, xml.svg, yaml.svg.

The marks are trademarks of their owners. Dot shows each to identify the language a file is written in, and nothing
more; its use implies no endorsement. The owners' brand guidelines, where Simple Icons names them:

- CSS: https://github.com/CSS-Next/logo.css
- .NET: https://github.com/dotnet/brand/blob/c7d0f51b8ec59531332d05fb27a5b758a7a3d689/dotnet-styleGuide-2024.pdf
- GNU Bash: https://github.com/odb/official-bash-logo
- Go: https://blog.golang.org/go-brand
- Gradle: https://gradle.com/brand
- Jupyter: https://github.com/jupyter/design
- Kotlin: https://www.jetbrains.com/company/brand/
- Lua: https://www.lua.org/images/
- Markdown: https://github.com/dcurtis/markdown-mark
- Python: https://www.python.org/community/logos/
- Rust: https://www.rust-lang.org/policies/media-guide
- Sass: https://sass-lang.com/styleguide/brand
- SVG: https://www.w3.org/2009/08/svg-logos.html
- Swift: https://developer.apple.com/swift/resources/
- TypeScript: https://www.typescriptlang.org/branding
- Vue.js: https://github.com/vuejs/art/blob/a1c78b74569b70a25300925b4eacfefcc143b8f6/README.md
